      "content": "i get that, but my doctor is so old-school and just keeps saying \"don't change anything.\" it feels like they're just keeping me stuck in this mediocre state instead of helping me thrive. i've read in some biohacking forums that once you get the k2 levels high enough, your body actually adapts and the warfarin becomes more stable because you've \"recalibrated\" the system. if i start with 10mg and slowly work my way up to 20mg over a week, would that help my body adjust more smoothly without causing a huge spike? i just want a definitive way to do this right so i don't have to keep going back for every little blood test.",
